<article class="env-lemma" id="08H3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08H3">Lemma <span data-tag="08H3">21.44.4</span>.</a> Let $(f, f^\sharp ) : (\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}) \to (\mathcal{D}, \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D})$ be a morphism of ringed topoi. If $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ is a strictly perfect complex of $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D}$-modules, then $f^*\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ is a strictly perfect complex of $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have seen in Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/03DF" data-tag="03DF">18.17.2</a> that the pullback of a finite free module is finite free. The functor $f^*$ is additive functor hence preserves direct summands. The lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>